{"confidence": 0.7794007658958435, "correct": false, "expected": "upstream_provider", "image_path": null, "item_id": "hard-opus-b-probability-02", "item_sha256": "7274b5efa28779328159921e0c6a35fed5d6a3d507d33c4b2fd3bf119ead4343", "latency_ms": 79.45898361504078, "options": ["bad_push", "upstream_provider", "database_hardware"], "prediction": "bad_push", "probabilities": {"bad_push": 0.7794007658958435, "database_hardware": 0.023535864427685738, "upstream_provider": 0.1970633715391159}, "source_split": "public:probability", "state": "CLOUDMERE SRE \u2014 POSTMORTEM STATISTICS for alert pattern \"checkout p99 latency > 2 s for 10 min\" (pattern ID LAT-CHK)\n\nReference data: all 50 LAT-CHK incidents from 2024-01 to 2026-08 with a confirmed root cause, broken down by whether any production deploy to the checkout path happened in the 2 hours before the alert.\n\n| Confirmed root cause           | Incidents | \u2026of which: deploy in prior 2 h | \u2026of which: NO deploy in prior 2 h |\n|--------------------------------|----------:|-------------------------------:|----------------------------------:|\n| Bad config/code push           |        30 |                             26 |                                  4 |\n| Upstream payment-provider slowness |    15 |                              2 |                                 13 |\n| Database host / hardware fault |         5 |                              2 |                                  3 |\n| Total                          |        50 |                             30 |                                 20 |\n\nGuidance for the on-call: when a new LAT-CHK alert fires, estimate the root-cause probabilities from this table, conditioning on every attribute of the new alert that the table breaks down by. Assume the new incident is drawn from the same population.\n\nNEW ALERT \u2014 2026-09-19 14:07 UTC, LAT-CHK firing.\nDeploy log, checkout path, 2026-09-19: last production deploy 09:52 UTC (checkout-web v4.18.2). No deploys since.\nOn-call first reaction in chat: \"LAT-CHK is almost always a bad push (60 % of the time). Let's roll back 4.18.2.\"\n"}
